Lemma: Let f, g : ℝ → ℝ differentiable on [0,T], f,g ≥ 0 on [0,T], g > 0 on (0,T), and f/g non-increasing on (0,T). Then F(r) = ∫_0^r f / ∫_0^r g is non-increasing on (0,T).

